  "summary": "Delight in the delicate elegance of traditional <b>French dumplings</b> featuring cold-smoked trout folded into a light choux paste. These airy quenelles are gently shaped using warm spoons before being poached in lightly salted simmering water until tender and fluffy. The smoky aroma of the fish pairs harmoniously with a silky sauce made from reduced white wine, rich butter, and chopped fresh chives. As the dumplings float gracefully in the hot poaching liquid, their texture transforms into a pillowy treat that melts in your mouth. Smoked seafood offers a distinct depth that elevates this classic bistro creation into an extraordinary dining experience. A splash of heavy cream enriches the herbal broth, highlighting the natural oils and delicate smoke of the fish without overwhelming it. Serve these hot dumplings in shallow bowls with crusty French bread to soak up every drop of aromatic broth. Ideal for elegant starter courses or light formal suppers.",
